      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 6 years 10 months ago",
      "body": "[QUOTE FROM ANOTHER POST]\nbridget said:\nMost of the time we just cook like at home, we have a tiny gas oven or in certain areas we use the fire place. It's very special to cook outdoors.\n[/QUOTE]\nThat depends on how many days you're going to spend during the hike. It would be better to take more food if you're planning a 3+ day trip. We have special camping cookware for such occasions, here's the\nreview\nabout it, it consists of portable gas oven, a kettle, pan and bowls. You don't actually need to carry all the pieces, just pack it according to the amount of food you will have.",
